{
 "id": "2026-10-21-storm-adam-spain-floods",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Six hundred millimeters of rain in thirty-six hours. Why did Spain flood so fast?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "AEMET, Spain's weather agency, says the town of Pego near Alicante got six hundred thirty-two millimeters in thirty-six hours. Several spots in Valencia and Alicante passed five hundred. The agency issued its highest red alert for the Valencia region."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Media report at least four dead. Pego's mayor said residents waited on rooftops, and helicopters lifted people to safety. Emergency units were deployed, and classes were suspended in dozens of municipalities."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Meteorologists call the system a DANA, an isolated high-altitude low, nicknamed Adam. Its remnants then hit southern France. Euronews reports one dead near Marseille and one missing in Corsica, with about two hundred millimeters in parts of the Gard."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Spain's coast see another flood this autumn? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
